<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#cowrie-shell">Glossary</a> · Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cowrie shell</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as cowrie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The cowrie shell is the shell of a small sea snail, used as currency across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. Cowries imported from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> became a standard currency in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> they facilitated market exchange across long distances, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a>'s tribute to Oyo included cowrie shells.</p></div>
